      "title": "The Double Alignment Problem: Civil-Military Relations in the Age of Artificial Intelligence",
      "summary": "<p>Artificial intelligence poses the greatest challenge to American civil-military relations since the advent of the nuclear bomb. AI plays outside the political bounds that contain other challenges, however odious. It compounds the inherent problem of civil-military relations &#8211; aligning the state and the military &#8211; with an additional alignment problem: that of human and agent. In doing so, AI threatens to undermine the constitutionalism and professionalism on which status quo civil-military relations depend. Nonetheless, artificial intelligence has developed so fast that the field of civil-military relations lags far behind it.&#160;What follows is an attempt to reckon with the implications of</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://warontherocks.com/the-double-alignment-problem-civil-military-relations-in-the-age-of-artificial-intelligence/\">The Double Alignment Problem: Civil-Military Relations in the Age of Artificial Intelligence</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://warontherocks.com\">War on the Rocks</a>.</p>",
